# ===========================================================================
# What git does not carry.
#
# THE RULE IS THE LEADING UNDERSCORE: a file or directory named _anything is
# scratch, and everything without one is the project. Two exceptions are
# spelled out below and both are directories that predate the rule.
#
# The rule is meant to be TOTAL — every file on disk should be either tracked
# or matched here, with nothing falling between — and there is a one-line
# check for that at the bottom.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UNSHIPPED IS NOT THE SAME AS DISPOSABLE. DO NOT BULK-DELETE BY THE PATTERN.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The underscore says "git does not carry this". It does not say "nobody needs
# this", and reading it as though it did is the mistake this paragraph exists
# to prevent. A one-shot probe whose question is now an assertion in
# scripts/test-engine.mjs is cheap to lose. A sketch that a source comment
# points at is not — deleting it strands the explanation and there is no
# command that rebuilds either one.
_*

# The hand layout, worked out at 6, 40 and 80 cards on a phone viewport before
# js/ui.js was written. NAMED IN A COMMENT INSIDE css/styles.css (:439), which
# is what makes it worth keeping on disk: the stylesheet explains a decision by
# pointing here. Unshipped — index.html never loads it — so it stays out of the
# repository, but it is not litter.
sketches/

# Per-machine editor and session state: launch settings, transcripts. None of
# it belongs to anybody else checking this out.
.claude/

# CAPTURED OUTPUT IS DELETED ON SIGHT, not kept. A redirected run log is a
# transcript of one execution of something that is still on disk and still
# runnable, so keeping it buys nothing and costs a stale copy — and a stale
# copy is worse than none, because it reads as evidence for a version of the
# code that no longer exists. Re-run the thing instead.
*.log
*.out

# OS and editor litter.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# THERE ARE NO DEPENDENCIES. package.json has no "dependencies" key, the page
# loads ES modules straight from js/, and the one third-party library (PeerJS)
# arrives as a pinned CDN tag in index.html. node_modules/ should therefore
# never exist; it is listed only so that a tool which creates one cannot get it
# committed by somebody who did not look.
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored, and deliberately so — everything in scripts/ that is not scratch:
#
#   scripts/test-engine.mjs   the suite itself
#   scripts/peershim.mjs      the transport the suite talks over, headless
#   scripts/gen-icons.js      generates icons/, which ships
#
# That list is hand-written, so treat it as a description rather than as the
# enforcement — a fourth keeper added to scripts/ will not appear in it on its
# own. What IS checkable is that nothing has fallen through the gap:
#
#     git ls-files --others --exclude-standard     # must print nothing
#
# Empty means every file on disk is either tracked or deliberately ignored. A
# line of output is either a project file nobody staged or scratch work missing
# its underscore, and those two look identical until somebody commits.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
